  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\nFrom {踏|ふ}む (to step on) - figuratively \"standing on\" something as a foundation\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{他動詞|たどうし} (transitive) - takes a を object\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{踏|ふ}まえて - based on ~, considering ~\n- 〜を{踏|ふ}まえた + noun - a ~ based on...\n\nREGISTER:\nOften used in formal or business contexts when discussing decisions or proposals based on certain factors.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {基|もと}づく - to be based on\n- {考慮|こうりょ}する - to consider\n- {前提|ぜんてい}とする - to premise on",
